---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="What is Wood Gasification | Smokeless Heat Blog" description="Learn how wood gasification works in Vedolux boilers for clean, efficient heating.">
  <Header />

  <main class="pt-24">
    <section class="py-16 bg-charcoal text-cream">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6">
        <p class="text-ember text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.3em] mb-4">January 17, 2009</p>
        <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl">What is Wood Gasification</h1>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="py-16 bg-cream">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6">
        <p class="text-lg text-charcoal/80 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          Wood gasification is a way of burning wood so cleanly that the chimney produces almost no smoke. Instead of just lighting a fire, the boiler first heats the wood with limited oxygen. This releases a flammable gas (called wood gas, holzgas, or producer gas) made mostly of carbon monoxide, hydrogen, and carbon dioxide. That gas is then pulled down into a second chamber and burned at roughly 2,000°F.
        </p>
        <p class="text-lg text-charcoal/80 leading-relaxed mb-10">
          The result is more heat from the same wood and far less smoke.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-darkwood mb-6">How it works in a Vedolux boiler</h2>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 text-charcoal/80 mb-10 space-y-3 text-lg">
          <li>Wood is loaded into the upper chamber.</li>
          <li>Heat and limited air release the wood gas.</li>
          <li>The gas is drawn down into the lower combustion chamber.</li>
          <li>It burns at very high temperature.</li>
          <li>Clean exhaust leaves the chimney — usually just heat shimmer or light steam, not smoke.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-darkwood mb-6">Why it matters</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-charcoal/80 mb-10 space-y-2 text-lg">
          <li>More usable heat from every load of wood</li>
          <li>Smoke-free operation once the fire is established</li>
          <li>Wood is a renewable fuel, similar to solar or wind</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-darkwood mb-6">Tips for best results</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-charcoal/80 mb-10 space-y-2 text-lg">
          <li>Aim for about 20% moisture content in Vedolux boilers</li>
          <li>Proper seasoning usually takes 12–18 months</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-darkwood mb-6">Typical composition of wood gas</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-charcoal/80 mb-12 space-y-2 text-lg">
          <li>51% Nitrogen (N₂)</li>
          <li>22% Carbon Monoxide (CO)</li>
          <li>18% Hydrogen (H₂)</li>
          <li>6% Carbon Dioxide (CO₂)</li>
          <li>3% Methane (CH₄)</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="aspect-video w-full overflow-hidden border border-wood/20">
          <iframe
            src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/TuI5f1-7K7Q"
            title="Infrared video of wood gasification"
            class="w-full h-full"
            frameborder="0"
            allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"
            allowfullscreen
          ></iframe>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-charcoal/50 text-center">
          Infrared video is compliments of Kembek LLC. Kembek LLC provides a full array of Industrial and Residential Infrared Services and Home Energy Audits customized to fit your needs.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
